<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RUT_StrandedDeformation.xml   UtinniPatches - MIASMA_FAUNA_FLOOR_ROSTER_1 /
  WARDEN_MOTHER_BEFRIENDING_1

  🔴 Fixes a dangling reference: RM_Miasma.xml's own RM_StrandingPoolsExtension
  block already names <strandedDeformationHediff>RUT_StrandedDeformation</strandedDeformationHediff>
  and RM_JobGiver_ReturnToWater.cs already reads it, but MEASURED this pass —
  the def itself was never authored anywhere in the repo. Correctness
  outranks seat ownership (CLAUDE.md): fixed on sight rather than filed.

  miasma_fauna_roster_2026-09-23.md §5: "gills going leathery, fins splaying
  into feet that don't quite work." Read as a mechanical condition on an
  ordinary nursery juvenile, per the owner's ruling that the stranded are the
  nursery's failures rather than their own species — never a bespoke
  creature. ⛔ Altering the juvenile's own SPRITE per that same section's
  "the look" row is NOT attempted here: how much a hediff can change an
  animal's rendered appearance is an engine question the roster's own text
  flags UNMEASURABLE on the Mac. This hediff is mechanical only (movement,
  survivability) — a visual pass is owed separately once that question has a
  Desktop answer.

  Permanent (initialSeverity == maxSeverity, not tendable, no immunity) —
  "does not thrive" per the roster, and the roster's own §5 table says the
  mechanism it replaces (RM_JobGiver_ReturnToWater) is deliberately
  SUPPRESSED for a carrier of this hediff, so there is no recovery path for
  this to represent.

  Move-speed and pain-threshold offsets are this pass's own INVENTED tuning,
  same magnitude class as RUT_FeverForged_Painworn (same folder) — "a
  half-working gait" as a real handicap without being an automatic death
  sentence, since roster §5 also says a stranded animal "occasionally
  survives into something that works."

  Carries RM_HediffCompProperties_LocatableCall (mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards)
  for the roster's "the young CALLS. Audible, locatable, and it does not
  stop" — kept generic on the hediff so every deformed stranded animal
  calls, regardless of which mechanism stranded it.
-->
<Defs>

  <HediffDef>
    <defName>RUT_StrandedDeformation</defName>
    <label>stranded deformation</label>
    <description>Gills gone leathery, fins splaying into feet that don't quite work. Whatever this creature was built to be, the muck had other ideas — it cannot return to open water, and it does not thrive there on land either. It calls, and it does not stop.</description>
    <hediffClass>Hediff</hediffClass>
    <isBad>true</isBad>
    <tendable>false</tendable>
    <initialSeverity>1</initialSeverity>
    <maxSeverity>1</maxSeverity>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <statOffsets>
          <MoveSpeed>-0.9</MoveSpeed>
          <PainShockThreshold>-0.1</PainShockThreshold>
        </statOffsets>
      </li>
    </stages>
    <comps>
      <li MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards" Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RM_HediffCompProperties_LocatableCall">
        <callSound>Pawn_Frog_Call</callSound>
        <callIntervalTicksRange>900~1500</callIntervalTicksRange>
      </li>
    </comps>
  </HediffDef>

</Defs>
